    "secondaryGap": "Single source (wikipron kat_geor_narrow, human, 20894) — but LARGE, and Georgian's one-letter-one-phoneme orthography means low referee-error risk. No kaikki per-language dump / epitran kat referee committed. The mapping is additionally the standard Georgian alphabet→IPA (any grammar), and the 33 letters were each derived from hundreds–thousands of aligned referee tokens, so the segmental inventory is strongly attested even from the one source.",
